{
  "info": {
    "name": "Hotel Offer Orchestrator",
    "description": "End-to-end checks for the Hotel Offer Orchestrator API.\n\nPick an environment (local or production) that sets `baseUrl`, then run the whole collection in order: later requests depend on earlier ones (cache hits after request 04, outages toggled in 11/14 and restored in 16/17).\n\nCLI: `npx --yes newman run postman/hotel-offer-orchestrator.postman_collection.json -e postman/local.postman_environment.json`\nProduction (allow for a cold start): add `-e postman/production.postman_environment.json --timeout-request 120000`.\n\nCovers: a city with overlapping hotels (delhi), price filtering in Redis, a city with no results (atlantis), validation errors, one supplier down (partial result + X-Failed-Suppliers) and both suppliers down (503).",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "01 Health check",
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "pm.test('status is 200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
              "const body = pm.response.json();",
              "pm.test('reports supplierA and supplierB', () => {",
              "  pm.expect(body).to.have.nested.property('suppliers.supplierA');",
              "  pm.expect(body).to.have.nested.property('suppliers.supplierB');",
              "});",
              "pm.test('reports redis and temporal', () => {",
              "  pm.expect(body).to.have.nested.property('dependencies.redis.status');",
              "  pm.expect(body).to.have.nested.property('dependencies.temporal.status');",
              "});"
            ]
          }
        }
      ],
      "request": {
        "method": "GET",
        "header": [],
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/health",
          "host": [
            "{{baseUrl}}"
          ],
          "path": [
            "health"
          ]
        },
        "description": "Reports both mock suppliers, Redis and Temporal. ok/degraded return 200, down returns 503."
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "02 Supplier A hotels (delhi)",
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "pm.test('status is 200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
              "const body = pm.response.json();",
              "pm.test('returns a non-empty array', () => pm.expect(body).to.be.an('array').that.is.not.empty);",
              "pm.test('items have hotelId, name, price, city, commissionPct', () => {",
              "  body.forEach((h) => pm.expect(h).to.include.all.keys('hotelId', 'name', 'price', 'city', 'commissionPct'));",
              "});",
              "pm.test('all items are in delhi', () => body.forEach((h) => pm.expect(h.city).to.eql('delhi')));"
            ]
          }
        }
      ],
      "request": {
        "method": "GET",
        "header": [],
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/supplierA/hotels?city=delhi",
          "host": [
            "{{baseUrl}}"
          ],
          "path": [
            "supplierA",
            "hotels"
          ],
          "query": [
            {
              "key": "city",
              "value": "delhi"
            }
          ]
        },
        "description": "Mock Supplier A API."
      }
    },
